From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team <oe.patch@openatv.example>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GLES: force the GLES2 renderer path on HiSilicon CV200

Kodi requests an EGL_CONTEXT_CLIENT_VERSION 2 context on the STB windowing
backend and is built with OPENGLES_FORCE_GLES2.  The HiSilicon CV200 Mali-T720
driver still reports "OpenGL ES 3.1" through GL_VERSION.  Kodi consequently
selects its GLES 3.1 shaders and texture handling at runtime, which renders
transparent GUI images with a black background while text remains correct.

Keep the actual driver string in the graphics log, but expose GLES 2.0 to
Kodi's renderer selection on the affected CV200 receivers.  Other HiSilicon
SoCs and hardware video composition remain unchanged.

diff --git a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
--- a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@ bool CRenderSystemGLES::InitRenderSystem()
       sscanf(ver, "%*s %*s %d.%d", &m_RenderVersionMajor, &m_RenderVersionMinor);
     m_RenderVersion = ver;
   }
+#if defined(TARGET_HISI_CV200)
+  if (m_RenderVersionMajor >= 3)
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+              "HiSilicon CV200 GLES compatibility: driver reports {}, forcing Kodi's GLES 2.0 "
+              "renderer path",
+              m_RenderVersion);
+    m_RenderVersionMajor = 2;
+    m_RenderVersionMinor = 0;
+  }
+#endif
 
   // Get our driver vendor and renderer
   const char *tmpVendor = (const char*) glGetString(GL_VENDOR);
-- 
